Article 3 The military facilities protection committee shall perform the following duties:
(1) Formulate measures for the protection of military facilities in accordance with the laws, regulations, and national policies and guidelines on the protection of military facilities;
(2) Organize and guide the protection of military facilities within its administrative area, and coordinate the resolution of matters concerning the protection of military facilities;
(3) Organize and carry out publicity and education on the protection of military facilities;
(4) Organize and carry out supervision and inspection of the implementation of laws and regulations on the protection of military facilities.

Article 27 For the purposes of the Law on the Protection of Military Facilities, military communication and power transmission lines include:
(1) Overhead lines: poles (towers), wires (cables), transformers, distribution rooms, and other ancillary facilities;
(2) Buried lines: underground or underwater electric (optical) cables, pipelines, inspection wells, boundary markers, submarine cable marker buoys, unattended carrier repeater stations, cable pressurization stations, and other ancillary facilities;
(3) Wireless lines: unattended microwave stations, microwave passive reflectors, antennas of various fixed radio stations (sites), and other ancillary facilities.

Article 42 Where personnel on duty of a military installation management unit encounter the illegal acts listed in Article 30 of the Military Installations Protection Law, they may take the following compulsory measures to stop them:
(1) expel persons who have illegally entered the military restricted zone from the military restricted zone;
(2) seize the equipment, tools or other articles used for committing the illegal act, detain persons whose illegal circumstances are serious, and immediately transfer them to the public security organ or the state security organ;
(3) in case of emergency, clear obstacles that seriously endanger the safety and operational effectiveness of military installations.
